{
  "name": "Ottoman kiosk",
  "_about": "THE K\u00d6\u015eK: a room W x L, H tall to the beam, on a platform `plat` high (steps up the front before each door), inside a colonnade G deep on all four sides (`ottoman` columns, nf across the front and ns along the sides, corners counted in both, a `beam` on them), the whole under one low hipped lead roof (pitch) whose deep eave reaches `eave` past the columns; windows all round every wB (wW wide), two doors in the front dX either side of the middle. `dome` yes sets a dome (domeR) on a drum over the room, up through the roof. The Audience Chamber (Arz Odas\u0131) is this with 22 columns; the Baghdad and Yerevan kiosks with the dome. (tools/archgen/ottoman.py)",
